   "text": {
    "L1": "A decimal place tells us the value of each digit.",
    "L2": "The ones place is the centre. There is no oneths place.",
    "L3": "Moving right, each place is one tenth of the place before it: tenths, hundredths, then thousandths.",
    "L4": "In 3.472, the digits mean 3 ones, 4 tenths, 7 hundredths and 2 thousandths.",
    "L5": "So 3.472 equals 3 plus 4 tenths plus 7 hundredths plus 2 thousandths.",
    "L6": "A digit's value depends on its place, not only on its face value.",
    "L7": "For example, in 0.19, 1 tenth is worth more than 9 hundredths.",
    "L8": "Now tap the value of the 2 in 5.27."
   },
